# H96 Max M9 / M9S deltas on top of
#   rockchip_defconfig + kernel/configs/android-14.config + rk3576.config
#
# Chosen by diffing the resulting .config against the stock 6.1.75 config
# extracted from the shipped boot.img.  Only real differences are listed:
# symbols that simply did not exist in 6.1.75, and the toolchain version
# strings, are left alone.
#
# The AIC8800 WiFi/BT driver is NOT configured here -- it is built as an
# external module out of kernel/rockchip/kernel-modules/wifi/aic8800, the
# way device/amlogic/g12-common builds its out-of-tree modules.

# Modules stock builds and then does not ship.  kernel.mk is not selective --
# every module the kernel builds lands in vendor_dlkm -- so unlike stock we pay
# for them: 5.5 MB of Broadcom driver for a chip this board does not have, and
# 4 MB of kernel headers nothing here reads.  Turning them off leaves
# vendor_dlkm holding exactly the five modules the stock image shipped.
# CONFIG_AP6XXX is not set
# CONFIG_IKHEADERS is not set

# Khadas Edge-2L hardware this board does not have.
# CONFIG_KHADAS_WATCHDOG is not set
# CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_HYN is not set
# CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX585 is not set
# CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX678 is not set
# CONFIG_VIDEO_OS08A10 is not set

# Debug options the Edge-2L defconfig carries and stock does not.
# CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_DRM_DEBUG is not set

# Codec for the Edge-2L, not for the ES8388 on this board.
# CONFIG_SND_SOC_RK730 is not set
